# Exceptions for .asset files such as lightning pre-baking
LightingData.asset     binary

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# *.asset is deliberately NOT given the unity-yaml macro above.
#
# That macro carries eol=lf, which normalises line endings even on files git
# detects as binary. Most .asset files are YAML under Force Text serialization,
# but some types - TerrainData above all - stay BINARY whatever the
# serialization mode. Applying eol=lf to those strips every CR byte out of the
# file and destroys it silently: the file still opens, still has a plausible
# size, and Unity simply refuses to import it.
#
# This project lost a sculpted 1025x1025 terrain heightmap that way on
# 2026-08-15. Assets/New Terrain 2.asset went into git 1,070 bytes short of the
# size its own header declared, and restoring it from the commit overwrote the
# only good copy. Assets/New Terrain.asset had already been damaged the same
# way, 59 bytes short, since the clone on 2026-07-28.
#
# Leaving the attribute off lets git auto-detect: YAML .asset files are handled
# as text, binary ones are left byte-for-byte alone. Do not add eol or text
# here without checking round-trip integrity on a binary .asset first.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.asset                 merge=unityyamlmerge linguist-language=yaml
